// v6.17.4: TRANSITION_WAIT overstay guard. WEAK-tier opposition (a lingering
// CHoCH-level warning or failed-continuation reading) has no natural time
// limit of its own -- XAU_AssessFailureAndSweep is a ROLLING lookback
// comparison, so a genuinely choppy/grinding market can keep re-triggering
// it bar after bar with no single break ever confirming a real reversal.
// Runtime-proven from the live journal: TRANSITION_WAIT observed holding for
// consecutive M5 bars with HTF_TREND_FOLLOW/TREND_PULLBACK withheld the
// entire time and zero setups scoring in either direction. This counts
// consecutive TRANSITION_WAIT bars (any cause) and forces a release to
// DIRECTION_BOTH_ALLOWED once InpMaxTransitionWaitBars is exceeded --
// "stay flat only briefly, with a clear reason" rather than indefinitely.
// Does NOT touch STRONG/MEDIUM confirmation thresholds; only ends indecision.
